      "type": "explain",
      "title": {
        "en": "German Umlauts & Special Characters"
      },
      "body": "German has 4 unique characters:\n\n- **Ä / ä**: Sounds like 'e' in 'pet' (*Käse* = cheese).\n- **Ö / ö**: Form 'o' with lips, say 'e' (*Öl* = oil).\n- **Ü / ü**: Form 'u' with lips, say 'i' (*über* = over).\n- **ß (Eszett / Sharp S)**: Sounds like a double 'ss' (*heiß* = hot). Never appears at start of words."
    },
